            <ArticleTitle>Understanding spirituality and spiritual care in nursing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7748/ns.2017.e10311</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spirituality is a complex concept that has different meanings for different people. Spiritual care is a fundamental aspect of nursing and attending to the spiritual needs of patients may improve their health outcomes. This article, the first in a series of three, explores various definitions of spirituality, and the importance of spirituality and spiritual care in healthcare settings. The second article of this series provides an in-depth exploration of the assessment of patients' spiritual care needs, and the third and final article in this short series discusses spiritual care nursing interventions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
